cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "OpenHawk: Physics-Based 3D Tennis Tracking from Broadcast Video"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Segan
    given-names: Max
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/maxsegan/openhawk"
version: "2026-09-29"
date-released: "2026-09-29"
abstract: >-
  Automatic reconstruction of 3D tennis ball flights, events and player positions from single
  broadcast videos: court and camera calibration, 2D ball tracking, event detection, and a
  whole-point physical fit with a 3D flight model and a court bounce law re-measured on
  Hawk-Eye data.
keywords:
  - tennis
  - computer vision
  - ball tracking
  - 3D reconstruction
  - sports physics
